                      <div class="itinerary-toggle-icon"></div>
                      <span>Day 2 — Cai Rang Floating Market · Fruit Orchard · Back to Saigon</span>
                    </summary>
                    <div class="premium-itinerary-content custom-blog-prose max-w-none">
                      <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-md mb-6 border border-slate-200">
                        <p class="font-bold text-slate-800 mb-2">Stage Highlights:</p>
                        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-slate-700 m-0 space-y-1">
                          <li>Sunrise boat cruise into Cai Rang Floating Market at its peak bustle</li>
                          <li>The Rice Travel Group dedicated photographer capturing candid moments</li>
                          <li>Hand-paddled sampan through shady green water coconut canals</li>
                          <li>Live UNESCO "Đờn Ca Tài Tử" folk performance & DIY Bánh Khọt workshop</li>
                        </ul>
                      </div>

                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>06:00 AM — Hotel Breakfast:</strong> Fuel up with a hearty breakfast at your hotel, saving energy for the most extraordinary morning of the expedition.</p>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>06:30 AM — Sunrise at Cai Rang Floating Market:</strong> Board your private boat and glide into Cai Rang Floating Market at its most alive hour. Hundreds of wooden boats loaded with fresh watermelons, pineapples, pumpkins, and dragon fruits weave past one another. Savor a steaming bowl of floating noodle soup or a cup of iced Vietnamese coffee right on the water.</p>

                      <div class="bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 my-4 rounded-r-md">
                        <p class="font-semibold text-amber-800 mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
                          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
                            <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M4 3a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V5a2 2 0 00-2-2H4zm12 12H4l4-8 3 6 2-4 3 6z" clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                          </svg>
                          Photographer In Action
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-amber-900 text-base m-0"><a href="https://maps.app.goo.gl/hQdTTGcC1nuAN3da7?g_st=ic" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="underline font-bold text-amber-900">The Rice Travel Group's</a> photographer accompanies you on the boat, capturing every glowing beam of sunrise on the water and your candid smiles amidst the floating market.</p>
                      </div>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>08:30 AM — Riverside Fruit Orchard & DIY Bánh Khọt:</strong> Leave the bustling market behind and enter a lush riverside fruit orchard. Pick ripe tropical fruits straight from the trees, paddle a small sampan through winding green canals, settle in for a soulful live "Đờn Ca Tài Tử" performance, then gather around the hearth to press and fry golden, crispy <em>bánh khọt</em> with your own hands.</p>
                      
                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>12:00 PM — Hearty Mekong Lunch:</strong> Enjoy a celebratory lunch filled with fresh regional specialties in the orchard pavilion.</p>

                      <p style="margin-bottom:14px"><strong>01:30 PM — Return to Ho Chi Minh City:</strong> The private van departs Can Tho on the expressway back to Saigon, arriving at your original pickup point between 04:30 PM and 05:00 PM. Full high-resolution photo collection delivered to your inbox shortly after!</p>
                    </div>
                  </details>

                </div>
